---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
	title="Kilnbook for schools and colleges"
	description="Booking and kiln firing software for school and college ceramics departments: wheel time between classes, firing queues for one or two kilns, and courses that follow the semester."
>
	<section class="band-dark page-hero">
		<div class="wrap">
			<p class="eyebrow">For schools &amp; colleges</p>
			<h1>Kilns, wheels and classes, on the semester timetable.</h1>
			<p class="lede narrow">
				For ceramics departments with one or two kilns and a room full of students. Students book a
				wheel between classes, log their work for the next firing, and you see every course roster in
				one place.
			</p>
			<a href="/contact" class="btn">Book a demo</a>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section section-alt">
		<div class="wrap">
			<p class="eyebrow">How it fits</p>
			<h2>Built for a studio that runs on a timetable</h2>
			<div class="cards">
				<div class="card">
					<h3>Wheel time between classes</h3>
					<p>
						Students reserve wheels, hand-building tables and the slab roller in one-hour blocks. You
						set how many hours each group gets and how far ahead they can book.
					</p>
					<a href="/features/wheel-time">Wheel and table booking</a>
				</div>
				<div class="card">
					<h3>Firings for one or two kilns</h3>
					<p>
						Students log a piece from their phone when it goes on the shelf. Each kiln keeps its own
						bisque and glaze queue, and a firing log with the date, cone and who loaded it.
					</p>
					<a href="/features/firings">How firing queues work</a>
				</div>
				<div class="card">
					<h3>Courses and rosters</h3>
					<p>
						Set up each course as a fixed series of sessions. Instructors get their own login with
						the day's roster and can mark attendance from the studio tablet.
					</p>
					<a href="/features/classes">Classes and packs</a>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="wrap section narrow">
		<h2>A semester in the ceramics room</h2>
		<p>
			Open studio hours fill up fast in the weeks before critiques. With wheel booking, students
			claim an hour between classes instead of waiting by the door, and freed-up slots appear on the
			calendar as soon as someone cancels. A tablet by the door lets students check in, so you always
			know who is in the room while the kilns are running.
		</p>
		<p>
			At the end of a firing, every student with work in the load gets a text with a photo of the
			shelf. Pieces left behind can trigger a reminder, which helps when the semester ends and the
			shelves need clearing.
		</p>

		<h2>Which plan fits a department</h2>
		<p>
			The Starter plan covers one kiln. The Studio plan covers up to 3 kilns, so a department with
			one or two kilns has room to add another. School ceramics programs get 30% off any plan.
			<a href="/pricing">Compare plans</a>.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section class="wrap section narrow">
		<h2>Questions departments ask</h2>
		<details>
			<summary>We have two kilns. Which plan do we need?</summary>
			<p>
				The Studio plan, which covers up to 3 kilns. If you only fire one kiln, the Starter plan
				covers it.
			</p>
		</details>
		<details>
			<summary>Is there a discount for schools?</summary>
			<p>
				Yes. Registered nonprofits and school ceramics programs get 30% off any plan. Mention it when
				you book a demo.
			</p>
		</details>
		<details>
			<summary>Can we try it before the semester starts?</summary>
			<p>
				You get 30 days on the Studio plan with no card. At the end you pick a plan or your account
				pauses. Nothing is deleted.
			</p>
		</details>
	</section>

	<section class="cta-band">
		<div class="wrap">
			<h2>Get your ceramics room off the sign-up sheet.</h2>
			<p>See how Kilnbook handles your kilns, wheels and courses before the next semester starts.</p>
			<a href="/contact" class="btn btn-dark">Book a demo</a>
		</div>
	</section>
</Base>
